It is unlawful for any person or entity to conduct, or permit to be conducted, on its property any activity including, but not limited to, parties, events, concerts, festivals, or any other activity at which amplified noise, amplified music, or amplified sounds are generated exceeding levels established pursuant to this code section. Any person or entity allowing or facilitating such conduct which results in a violation of this code section shall be equally in violation as those actually responsible for generating the noise, and shall be deemed a party to the commissioner of a crime and may be charged with and convicted of said violation. A person that is "a party to the commission of a crime" shall be defined as:
(1) Directly commits the crime;
(2) Intentionally causes another person to commit the crime under such circumstances that the other person is not guilty of any crime, either in fact or legal incapacity;
(3) Intentionally aids, abets, or allows the commissioner of the crime; or
(4) Intentionally advises, encourages, hires, counsels, or approves another to commit the crime.
(Ord. of 08-12-2021 (1))

